## Start from scratch

You need [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/){% if with_frontend %}, [Node 26](https://nodejs.org){% endif %}{% if with_database %} and [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/){% endif %}. Then:

```bash
make doctor   # checks the tools and says how to fix what is missing
make setup    # installs everything{% if with_database %}, starts PostgreSQL on :{{ postgres_port }}, migrates{% endif %}
make dev      # API on http://127.0.0.1:8000/api{% if with_frontend %}, visor on http://127.0.0.1:5173{% endif %}
```

The API documentation is at http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs while `make dev` runs. Nothing needs
credentials locally: Logfire sends nothing without a token{% if with_database %}, and the database is the local container{% endif %}.
Optional local settings: `backend/.env.example`{% if with_frontend %} and `frontend/.env.example`{% endif %}.

