## Accounts

Accounts live in the project's PostgreSQL. There is no sign-up page: create them with the CLI,
which reads the password from standard input so that it stays out of the shell's history:

```bash
cd backend
printf '%s\n' "$PASSWORD" | uv run {{ project_slug }} users create --email you@example.com --admin
uv run {{ project_slug }} api-keys create --email you@example.com --name my-script   # printed once
```

{% if with_frontend %}The visor shows a sign-in form until someone is signed in, and `/api/messages`, the example
route, answers only signed-in users. {% endif %}A browser signs in with `POST /api/auth/login` and then holds an
HttpOnly session cookie (7 days without use or 30 in total end it). Scripts send an API key as
`Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
`users set-password`, `users deactivate`, `api-keys list` and `api-keys revoke` do the rest; `--help`
explains each one. Ten wrong passwords in a row pause an account's sign-in for a minute per attempt.
{%- endif %}

## Deploy

Pushing to `main` deploys; the CI must pass first. These one-time steps connect the services.
None of them is needed to develop locally.
{%- if with_database %}

**Database (Neon).** Create a project at https://console.neon.tech in an EU region (Frankfurt,
`aws-eu-central-1`). Copy two connection strings from "Connect": the **direct** one, and the
**pooled** one (host with `-pooler`).
{%- endif %}

**Logfire.** Create a project at https://logfire.pydantic.dev. Create a **write token** (Settings →
Write tokens) for the API's `LOGFIRE_TOKEN`, and a **read token** (Settings → Read tokens) for
`{{ project_slug }} obs status`: save it in `~/.config/{{ project_slug }}/logfire-read-token` or export it as `LOGFIRE_READ_TOKEN`.
{%- if with_frontend %} For browser errors,
create a frontend application in the project (Frontend → Applications) and set the two values it generates in Vercel:
its restricted token as `VITE_LOGFIRE_TOKEN` and the URL of the project's region as `VITE_LOGFIRE_BASE_URL`.{% endif %}
{%- if api_deploy == 'render' %}

**API (Render).** Dashboard → New → Blueprint → this repository. Render reads `render.yaml`
(Docker, Frankfurt, free plan, health check `/api/healthz`) and asks for the secrets: {% if with_database %}`DATABASE_URL`
(Neon, direct) and {% endif %}`LOGFIRE_TOKEN`. Its URL will be `https://{{ project_slug }}-api.onrender.com` unless the name
is taken.{% if with_database %} Migrations run at start-up. The free plan sleeps after 15 idle minutes; the first request then takes about a minute.{% endif %}
{%- elif api_deploy == 'railway' %}

**API (Railway).** Install the [Railway CLI](https://docs.railway.com/cli), then from the
repository root: `npm install --prefix .railway`, `railway login`, `railway link` (pick or create
the project), `railway config plan` and `railway config apply`. Then, in the Railway dashboard,
set {% if with_database %}`DATABASE_URL` (Neon, direct; or add a Railway PostgreSQL and reference it) and {% endif %}`LOGFIRE_TOKEN`,
generate a public domain for the service, and turn on "Wait for CI" in its settings.{% if with_database %} Migrations run as the pre-deploy command.{% endif %}
{%- elif api_deploy == 'fastapi_cloud' %}

**API (FastAPI Cloud).** `cd backend && uv run fastapi login`, then `uv run fastapi deploy` once to
create the app (name it `{{ project_slug }}`: its URL becomes `https://{{ project_slug }}.fastapicloud.dev`), then `uv run fastapi cloud setup-ci --secrets-only` to store `FASTAPI_CLOUD_TOKEN` and
`FASTAPI_CLOUD_APP_ID` in GitHub (`.github/workflows/deploy-api.yml` deploys on every green `main`).
Set the secrets: {% if with_database %}`uv run fastapi cloud env set --secret DATABASE_URL "<Neon direct URL>"` and {% endif %}`uv run fastapi cloud env set --secret LOGFIRE_TOKEN "<write token>"`,
plus `uv run fastapi cloud env set {{ env_prefix }}ENVIRONMENT production`.{% if with_database %} Migrations run at start-up.{% endif %}
{%- elif api_deploy == 'vercel' %}

**Visor and API (Vercel).** Import the repository at https://vercel.com/new (root directory: the
repository root; Vercel reads the services from `vercel.json`, region `fra1`). Add the
environment variables {% if with_database %}`DATABASE_URL` (Neon, **pooled**) and {% endif %}`LOGFIRE_TOKEN` for Production and Preview.
{%- if with_database %}
Production deploys come from `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (migrate, then deploy), not from the
Git integration: run `vercel link` locally and add the repository secrets `DATABASE_URL` (Neon,
**direct**), `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `VERCEL_ORG_ID` and `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID` (the last two are in `.vercel/project.json`).
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if with_frontend and api_deploy != 'vercel' %}

**Visor (Vercel).** Import the repository at https://vercel.com/new with root directory
`frontend`. `frontend/vercel.json` proxies `/api` to `{{ api_public_url }}`: if the API's real URL is
different, change it there. Web Analytics: turn it on in the project (no cookies).
{%- endif %}

**GitHub.** Protect `main`: require pull requests and the checks `Backend` and `Frontend`, and
allow auto-merge (Settings → General → "Allow auto-merge").

{%- if auth == 'sessions' %}

**First administrator.** Once the API is deployed, create it against the production database:
`printf '%s\n' "$PASSWORD" | DATABASE_URL="<Neon direct URL>" uv run {{ project_slug }} users create --email … --admin` from `backend/`.
{%- endif %}

**After a deploy.** `cd backend && uv run {{ project_slug }} obs status --commit <sha> --wait 15` says when the commit is live
and lists any error since.

